## SQ-SPFX-01
@group A
@commands full pack with `immersive-portals-2.3.7`, `portalgun`, `portalgels` kept in srv/mods; boot; `grep -E "Immersive Portals overwrites conform\|MixinChunkMap_C" logs/latest.log logs/debug.log \| head`; then a second boot with Immersive Portals and Portal Gun moved out
@pass first boot reaches `Done (` (world created), one `[compat] Immersive Portals overwrites conform to target visibility` line, one `Static binding violation ... m_183760_ in imm_ptl.mixins.json:common.chunk_sync.MixinChunkMap_C` WARN, no `Mixin apply failed ... MixinChunkMap_C`; second boot: no `[compat] Immersive Portals` line, Done
@fails `[compat] imm_ptl.mixins.json not found` / `could not set conformVisibility` (Mixin internals differ); IP outside `[2.3.7,2.4)` (one "outside the tested range" warning); another IP overwrite clashes with an access transformer (read the crash: the method name). Rewritten 2026-11-07 for the acceptTargets fix (the preApply fix FAILED r1106spfx)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject Mixin apply failed.*MixinChunkMap_C
bootreject imm_ptl\.mixins\.json not found|could not set conformVisibility
shell test "$(cat logs/latest.log logs/debug.log 2>/dev/null | grep -c "Immersive Portals overwrites conform to target visibility")" -ge 1 && echo "conform line present"
shell grep -hE "Immersive Portals overwrites conform|MixinChunkMap_C|outside the tested range" logs/latest.log logs/debug.log 2>/dev/null | head -6 | cut -c1-240; true
look one conform line and one Static binding violation WARN naming m_183760_ in MixinChunkMap_C; the second boot (Immersive Portals and Portal Gun moved out of srv/mods) is a separate boot: Done and no [compat] Immersive Portals line (bootreject on that boot)
## SQ-SPFX-02 | horror lasagna sequenced assembly in the full pack
@group A
@commands full pack: `/cdevtest rdetail horror_lasagna_sequenced_assembly`; `grep -h "horror_lasagna" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log \| grep -iE "error\|fail"`; spout + deployer rig is CQ-SPFX-01
@pass the recipe `creativedelight:createsequencedassembly/horror_lasagna_sequenced_assembly` is listed with 7 steps, the filling step names `create_central_kitchen:tomato_sauce` 250 mB, result 2 `brewinandchewin:horror_lasagna`; 0 error lines
@fails `brewinandchewin/recipes.js` guard `global.has(f.tomato_sauce)` false in the full pack (Central Kitchen id changed)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1106spfx/a1.qb
> cdevtest rdetail horror_lasagna_sequenced_assembly
expect verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:createsequencedassembly/horror_lasagna_sequenced_assembly serializer=\S+ result=brewinandchewin:horror_lasagna\*2\b
count verb=rdetail id=creativedelight:createsequencedassembly/horror_lasagna_sequenced_assembly part=step\d+ >= 7
expect tomato_sauce
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
shell grep -h "horror_lasagna" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|fail" | head -5; echo "errlines=$(grep -h horror_lasagna logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log | grep -ciE 'error|fail')"
look the step lines: the filling step names create_central_kitchen:tomato_sauce 250 mB (fields or step value); errlines=0

## SQ-SPFX-03
@group A + chain
@commands (a) full pack with `tools/scratch_query/nch_empty_fluid_probe.js` copied to `srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_nch_probe.js`: `grep "\[zqnch\]" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "zz_probe_empty_fluid" logs/kubejs/server.log`; (b) port chain p1 (`tools/scratch_query/batches/r1106cbp/run_boots.sh '^p1$'` with the 22:07 Common, CD, CB copied into CEPortTesting): `grep -h "horror_lasagna" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log`
@pass (a) `[zqnch] zz_probe_empty_fluid: skipped (... minecraft:empty ...)`, `[zqnch] zz_probe_good: built`, no `Error parsing recipe` naming `zz_probe` and no loose `create:kjs_` filling recipe; (b) no `Error parsing recipe ...horror_lasagna`, `with 0 failed recipes`
@fails `NCH._stepJsonHasEmptyFluid` (step `serialize()` / `json` not reachable in kubejs 1902.6: print `step.json` in the probe); `dropSteps` (newRecipe)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[zqnch\] zz_probe_empty_fluid: skipped .*minecraft:empty
bootexpect \[zqnch\] zz_probe_good: built
bootreject Error parsing recipe.*zz_probe
> cdevtest recipes create:kjs_ max=500
> cdevtest recipes zz_probe max=50
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0
shell echo "zz_probe_empty_fluid lines: $(grep -c zz_probe_empty_fluid logs/kubejs/server.log)"
look the create:kjs_ and zz_probe recipe lines: no loose create:kjs_ filling recipe from the probe, zz_probe_good present; (b) the port chain p1 half (run_boots.sh '^p1$' in batches/r1106cbp: no Error parsing recipe ...horror_lasagna, "with 0 failed recipes") is a chain boot of its own
